{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},"metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"HTTPDestinations","externalID":"HTTPDestinations","symbolKind":"module"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"anchor":"Sending-batches","title":"Sending batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch"],"anchor":"Encoding-a-batch","title":"Encoding a batch"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchRequests","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/SkippedRecord"],"anchor":"Splitting-a-batch-into-requests","title":"Splitting a batch into requests"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"],"anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts","title":"Waiting between attempts"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError"],"anchor":"Sending-requests","title":"Sending requests"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as the requests its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" splits it into: one request for an endpoint without limits. Each body is whatever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the encoder writes for its records, so events need no "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance and the wire format is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yours. It sends with "},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" by default, or through any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" you pass."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","isActive":true},{"text":": 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"text":" as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","isActive":true},{"text":", as is each record the encoder leaves out","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its requests.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of each request’s first record into its header","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"text":" is always the encoder’s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, give the destination a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for PostHog,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"make it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken:host:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"). To read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events inside the app or in a test, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destinations"},{"type":"text","text":") instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    func requests(for batch: [EventRecord]) -> BatchRequests<Never> {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        let body = EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","        return BatchRequests(requests: [EncodedRequest(body: body, recordIDs: batch.map(\\.id))], skippedRecords: [])","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers this destination beside the others, and what a delivery does while a batch is retried.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/InvalidBackoff":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"InvalidBackoff","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"InvalidBackoff","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InvalidBackoff","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/init(initialDelay:maximumDelay:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" throws for an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"initial delay that isn’t positive, or a maximum delay less than it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/invalidbackoff"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/SkippedRecord":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SkippedRecord"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/SkippedRecord","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A record a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" left out of a batch’s requests, and why."}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/skippedrecord","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SkippedRecord"}],"title":"SkippedRecord"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder/requests(for:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder\/requests(for:)","abstract":[{"text":"The requests that carry ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference"},{"text":" sends one after another, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records left out of them.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"requests","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"for","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","text":"EventRecord","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) ","kind":"text"},